{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>When you lift its fat from it.</b> After you lift the terumah of the tithe from it." "<b>And it shall be reckoned</b> — the remainder to the Levites as fully unconsecrated." "<b>Like the produce of the threshing floor, for Israel</b> — so that you not say: since Scripture calls it terumah — as it says ״כִּי אֶת מַעְשַׂר בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל אֲשֶׁר יָרִימוּ לַה׳ תְּרוּמָה״ — one might think it is all forbidden; therefore it says ״וְנֶחְשַׁב לַלְוִיִּם כִּתְבוּאַת גֹּרֶן״: just as that of Israel is unconsecrated, so too that of the Levite is unconsecrated (see Sifrei)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:11:36.186296903Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}